.TH YTRAN 1 "May 2026" "ytran 1.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
ytran \- fetch and summarize YouTube video transcripts
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ytran
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.RI [ VIDEO_URL_OR_ID " ..." ]
.br
.B ytran
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.RI CHANNEL_URL
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B ytran
fetches YouTube video transcripts via transcriptapi.com, formats them
with Claude or DeepSeek, generates summaries, and stores everything in a local
SQLite database.
.PP
When given a channel URL (containing \fB/@\fR, \fB/channel/\fR, \fB/c/\fR,
or \fB/user/\fR), the tool expands the full video list via
.BR yt\-dlp ,
skips already-downloaded videos, and processes the remainder with
automatic retry and exponential backoff.
.PP
Multiple video URLs are also processed in batch mode with backoff.
Failed downloads are re-queued at the back of the list (circular queue)
and retried until 4 consecutive failures at the backoff ceiling.
.SH CONFIGURATION
.PP
Configuration lives in
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/ytran/
(default
.IR ~/.config/ytran/ ).
.SS Default model
.PP
.I ~/.config/ytran/default
contains a single shortname (a section name from the models file):
.PP
.RS
.nf
\fBpro\fR
.fi
.RE
.PP
If absent, the compiled default
.RB ( claude-sonnet-4-6 )
is used.
.SS Model definitions
.PP
.I ~/.config/ytran/models
defines each model in INI-style sections:
.PP
.RS
.nf
\fB[pro]
name = deepseek-v4-pro
endpoint = https://api.deepseek.com/anthropic/v1/messages
api_key_file = .deepseek_api_key
input_price = 0.55
output_price = 2.19

[sonnet]
name = claude-sonnet-4-6
api_key_file = .anthropic_api_key
input_price = 3.0
output_price = 15.0\fR
.fi
.RE
.PP
Fields per section:
.TP
.B name
Full model string sent to the API (defaults to section name).
.TP
.B endpoint
API endpoint URL (auto-detected from name prefix if absent:
.B deepseek-
→ DeepSeek,
.B claude-
→ Anthropic).
.TP
.B api_key
Raw API key string.
.TP
.B api_key_file
Path to key file (resolved against
.B $HOME
if relative).
.TP
.B input_price ", " cache_write_price ", " cache_read_price ", " output_price
Pricing in $/MTok for cost tracking (falls back to compiled defaults).
.PP
All fields are optional.
CLI flags
.RB ( \-\-model ", " \-\-api-key )
override config values.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-b ", " \-\-browse
Open an interactive browser for the transcript database after processing
any URLs given on the command line.
Videos are shown sorted by
.B updated_at DESC
(most recently modified first).
If invoked with no arguments,
.B \-\-browse
is implied.
Options and URLs may be intermixed in any order.
.TP
.B \-\-fix
Scan all database entries and fill in any missing fields (metadata,
transcripts, summaries).
Uses circular retry queue with backoff for transient failures.
Entries saved with
.B \-\-no\-summary
are skipped; use
.B \-\-full
to include them.
.TP
.BR \-\-full " (" \-F )
Like
.BR \-\-fix ,
but includes raw\-only entries (those saved with
.BR \-\-no\-summary ).
The raw\-only flag is cleared and summaries are generated.
.PP
When given video URLs or IDs as arguments, only those specific
videos are processed.
Without arguments, the entire database is scanned.
Multiple videos use batch mode with backoff.
.TP
.BI \-\-max\-backoff " SECS"
Backoff ceiling in seconds for batch/fix/channel modes.
Default: 1800 (30 minutes).
.TP
.BI \-\-min\-delay " SECS"
Minimum delay between requests in batch modes.
Default: 5.
.TP
.BI \-\-initial\-delay " SECS"
Starting delay between requests in batch modes.
Default: 10.
.TP
.B \-\-opus
Use claude-opus-4-8 for formatting and summarization.
Shorthand for
.BR "\-\-model claude-opus-4-8" .
.TP
.B \-\-fable
Use claude-fable-5 for formatting and summarization.
Shorthand for
.BR "\-\-model claude-fable-5" .
.TP
.B \-\-haiku
Use claude-haiku-4-5 for formatting and summarization.
Shorthand for
.BR "\-\-model claude-haiku-4-5" .
.TP
.B \-\-sonnet
Use claude-sonnet-4-6 for formatting and summarization.
Shorthand for
.BR "\-\-model claude-sonnet-4-6" .
.TP
.B \-\-flash
Use deepseek-v4-flash for formatting and summarization.
Shorthand for
.BR "\-\-model deepseek-v4-flash" .
.TP
.B \-\-pro
Use deepseek-v4-pro for formatting and summarization (default).
Shorthand for
.BR "\-\-model deepseek-v4-pro" .
.TP
.BI \-\-model " MODEL"
Model to use for formatting and summarization.
Default: deepseek-v4-pro.
.TP
.BI \-\-api-key " FILE"
Override the API key file (default is auto-detected from model:
.B ~/.deepseek_api_key
for DeepSeek models,
.B ~/.anthropic_api_key
for Claude models).
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-no\-summary
Fetch metadata and raw transcript only; do not format or summarize
with Claude or DeepSeek.
The entry is flagged as raw\-only so that future
.B \-\-fix
runs leave it alone.
Does not require an LLM API key.
.TP
.BI \-\-skip " ID1,ID2,..."
Comma-separated list of video IDs to skip during batch operations
.RB ( \-\-fix ", " \-\-full ", channel, or multi-URL downloads).
.TP
.BR \-\-version " (" \-V )
Print version and exit.
.SH BATCH MODES
.PP
Three modes use the circular retry queue with AIMD
(additive decrease, multiplicative increase) backoff:
.TP
.B \-\-fix
Re-queues transient failures; marks permanent failures in the database.
Resumes from last position on restart via the
.I queue_state
table.
.TP
.B Channel URLs
Expands channel playlists via
.BR yt\-dlp (1),
filters already-downloaded videos, then processes the remainder.
Transcripts are fetched in
.B \-\-no\-summary
mode.
.TP
.B Multiple video URLs
Two or more video URLs on the command line trigger batch processing
with backoff.
.PP
On success, the delay decreases by 2 seconds (floor:
.BR \-\-min\-delay ).
On failure, the delay triples (ceiling:
.BR \-\-max\-backoff ).
After 4 consecutive failures at the ceiling, the tool gives up and
marks remaining videos with the last error detail.
.PP
Ctrl-C during batch processing saves the cursor position so the
next run resumes where it left off.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/ytran/youtube-transcripts.db
Default database location (respects $XDG_DATA_HOME).
.TP
.I ~/.youtubetotranscript_api_key
transcriptapi.com bearer token.
.TP
.I ~/.deepseek_api_key
DeepSeek API key (used when model starts with
.BR deepseek- ).
.TP
.I ~/.anthropic_api_key
Anthropic API key (used when model starts with
.BR claude- ).
.TP
.I ~/.config/ytran/default
Contains the default model shortname (e.g.,
.BR pro ).
.TP
.I ~/.config/ytran/models
INI-style model definitions (endpoint, key, pricing per model).
.SH DATABASE
The database at
.I ~/.local/share/ytran/youtube-transcripts.db
contains the following tables:
.TP
.B videos
One row per video. Three timestamp columns track the video lifecycle:
.BR "upload_date" " (YouTube's date),"
.BR "fetched_at" " (first download by ytran), and"
.BR "updated_at" " (last modified by --fix/--full)."
.B updated_at
is seeded from
.B fetched_at
on first download and bumped whenever
.B \-\-fix
or
.B \-\-full
generates new content.
.TP
.B channel_names
Historical channel name and handle tracking.
.TP
.B channels
Per-channel flags (e.g.,
.BR bulkdl ).
.TP
.B queue_state
Cursor position for resuming interrupted batch operations.
.TP
.B _browse_config
browse-sqlite3 display preferences, including the default sort
.BR "row_sort:videos = [[\"updated_at\",\"DESC\"]]" .
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR yt\-dlp (1)
\(em used for expanding channel URLs to video lists.
